Dadhimukha bows to Rāma Lakṣmaṇa Sugrīva and flies to Madhuvana --- Dadhimukha folds hands and tells Aṅgada Sugrīva feels no anger --- Dadhimukha bids Aṅgada bring all monkeys quickly to Sugrīva --- Aṅgada suspects Rāma heard news and bids hosts depart at once --- Monkeys praise Aṅgada humility and vow to follow him --- Aṅgada leaps skyward and all roaring hosts follow to Kiṣkindhā --- Sugrīva comforts grieving Rāma that Sītā is surely seen --- Sugrīva cites Jāmbavān Aṅgada Hanumān as pledge of success --- Hanumān bows and reports intact Sītā while Rāma honors him
